            "text": "An electronic load on a 500 mA supply"
          },
          {
            "id": "an2",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -11,
            "text": "The load draws a set current from the rails — 250 mA here — and shows the volts,",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an3",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -9.2,
            "text": "amps and watts while the circuit runs (Spice Lite). Raise it in its Properties",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an4",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -7.4,
            "text": "past the supply's 500 mA limit and the supply droops: the LED dims, the load",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an5",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -5.6,
            "text": "reads UNREG (it can no longer draw what it is set to), and the supply's own",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an6",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -3.8,
            "text": "readout turns amber. CR mode makes it a resistor instead.",
            "color": "#808080"
          }
